usique concrète","n":1}],"labels":[],"album_labels":[],"own_scenes":[],"scenes":[{"id":145647343892302,"name":"Música industrial","book":"A History of Rock Music 1951-2000","author":"Piero Scaruffi","start":1977,"end":1992,"desc":"El término lo usa por primera vez Monte Cazazza, pero su significado se define en Sheffield: Throbbing Gristle y Cabaret Voltaire usan el ruido de la fábrica como metáfora de la condición humana a finales del siglo XX. Throbbing Gristle (Second Annual Report, «música de la fábrica de la muerte»; 20 Jazz Funk Greats abre la puerta al industrial bailable y al synth-pop), Cabaret Voltaire, Clock DVA. Con los sellos independientes, la diversificación: Nurse With Wound, Zoviet France, This Heat, 23 Skidoo, Current 93 (y su folk apocalíptico), Hafler Trio, Coil, Psychic TV, Test Dept, Lustmord. Desde Australia, Foetus, el primer compositor «clásico» de la civilización punk (Hole, Nail, Thaw). En EE UU, Arcane Device y Controlled Bleeding.","color":"#94a3b8","family":"Gótico e industrial","link":"https://volteret4.github.io/scaruffi/#industrial"},{"id":44484960418276,"name":"Esoterismo post-industrial","book":"Loops 1 y 2. Una historia de la música electrónica","author":"Javier Blánquez (ed.)","start":1979,"end":2002,"desc":"Francotiradores inclasificables adoptados por la escena industrial que hicieron del ruido algo onírico y surreal: Coil (magia crowleyana, fantasías homoeróticas, «una mezcla de electricidad y drogas»), Psychic TV y su secta Thee Temple ov Psychick Youth, Nurse With Wound (krautrock + surrealismo), Current 93 (cut-up y folk) y el catalán Jordi Valls con Vagina Dentata Organ.","color":"#94a3b8","family":"Industrial y ruido","link":"https://volteret4.github.io/loops_timeline/#post-industrial"}],"book_tracks":[{"id":241140321895596,"artist":"Current 93","artist_id":63491385454844,"title":"Nature Unveiled","year":1984,"ess":0,"yt":"PcmOAnx7srM","kind":"a","book":{"id":8,"title":"A History of Rock Music 1951-2000","author":"Piero Scaruffi","url":"https://volteret4.github.io/scaruffi/"},"scene":"Música industrial","scene_id":145647343892302,"scene_link":"https://volteret4.github.io/scaruffi/#industrial","chapters":["Sección 5.8"],"pages":[[1,139,null]]},{"id":247655353444164,"artist":"Current 93","artist_id":63491385454844,"title":"Dogs Blood Rising","year":1985,"ess":0,"yt":"Zw-nlb39uIQ","kind":"a","book":{"id":8,"title":"A History of Rock Music 1951-2000","author":"Piero Scaruffi","url":"https://volteret4.github.io/scaruffi/"},"scene":"Música industrial","scene_id":145647343892302,"scene_link":"https://volteret4.github.io/scaruffi/#industrial","chapters":["Sección 5.8"],"pages":[[1,139,null]]},{"id":130345483474681,"artist":"Current 93","artist_id":63491385454844,"title":"Imperium","year":1987,"ess":0,"yt":"8N5fxgiN2_w","kind":"a","book":{"id":8,"title":"A History of Rock Music 1951-2000","author":"Piero Scaruffi","url":"https://volteret4.github.io/scaruffi/"},"scene":"Música industrial","scene_id":145647343892302,"scene_link":"https://volteret4.github.io/scaruffi/#industrial","chapters":["Sección 5.8"],"pages":[[1,139,null]]},{"id":209174038561888,"artist":"Current 93","artist_id":63491385454844,"title":"Thunder Perfect Mind","year":1992,"ess":0,"yt":"OriadJyatNg","kind":"a","book":{"id":8,"title":"A History of Rock Music 1951-2000","author":"Piero Scaruffi","url":"https://volteret4.github.io/scaruffi/"},"scene":"Música industrial","scene_id":145647343892302,"scene_link":"https://volteret4.github.io/scaruffi/#industrial","chapters":["Sección 5.8"],"pages":[[1,139,null]]},{"id":218164466135798,"artist":"Current 93","artist_id":63491385454844,"title":"Hitler As Kalki","year":null,"ess":0,"yt":"TuNZbcJB26g","kind":"s","book":{"id":8,"title":"A History of Rock Music 1951-2000","author":"Piero Scaruffi","url":"https://volteret4.github.io/scaruffi/"},"scene":"Música industrial","scene_id":145647343892302,"scene_link":"https://volteret4.github.io/scaruffi/#industrial","chapters":["Sección 5.8"],"pages":[[1,139,null]]}],"mentions":[{"book":"A History of Rock Music 1951-2000","author":"Piero Scaruffi","page":138,"text":"…With Wound, Zoviet France); some were experimenting with rhythm and texture (This Heat, 23 Skidoo, Hula); some were adopting an esoteric stance (Current 93, Hafler Trio, Psychic Tv, Coil); some were weaving static sheets of drones (Dome, i.e. former Wire 138"},{"book":"A History of Rock Music 1951-2000","author":"Piero Scaruffi","page":139,"text":"…harked back to the satirical and iconoclastic experiments of Dadaism and Futurism. His early, formative works (frequently shared with David Tibet of Current 93), such as Homotopy To Marie (1982) and Sylvie And Babs (1985), were similar in spirit to the Fugs' Virgin Forest, to Frank Zappa's breakneck…"},{"book":"A History of Rock Music 1951-2000","author":"Piero Scaruffi","page":139,"text":"…employed Tibetan percussions and electronic noise, and finally with the dub-funk percussive monster Urban Gamelan (1984). David Tibet's project, Current 93 (2), that often employed Nurse With Wound's Steve Stapleton, Coil's John Balance and/or 23 Skidoo's Fritz Haaman, centered on lugubrious ceremonies.…"},{"book":"A History of Rock Music 1951-2000","author":"Piero Scaruffi","page":212,"text":"…of terrorism in music. Apocalyptic Folk A notable exception within the ranks of industrial music came from the musicians who, led by David Tibet's Current 93, moved away from industrial music and ventured into a new form of folk, no less ominous and depressed. That \"apocalyptic folk\" was industrial…"}],"podcast":[],"awards":[],"concerts":[],"xref":[],"charts":[{"id":241140321895596,"type":"album","name":"Nature Unveiled","list_id":4389278164509,"list":"Music Genre Tree","src":"musthear","rank":603,"year":1984,"note":null,"yt":"SBpeT1AN6dU","scaruffi":7.5},{"id":241140321895596,"type":"album","name":"Nature Unveiled","list_id":71422834352820,"list":"RYM Top — Ambient — Ritual Ambient","src":"musthear","rank":30,"year":198